  "course_description": "This course explores the history of Latin America from European contact to present. Major themes include Latin America's position in a wider world; class, ethnic, and race relations; state-society relations; the making of regional and national identities.",
  "course_notes": "This course surveys Latin American history from the pre-Columbian era to the twenty-first century. Together, we will examine how people across the region experienced conquest, colonization, slavery, independence, revolution, and dictatorship as connected processes that extended beyond national boundaries. We will approach Latin American history through two key lenses: first, we examine how ¿Latin America¿ itself has been constructed and contested by different actors over time; second, we focus on how people have used everyday practices to navigate and challenge social hierarchies while shaping their own identities across borders.",
